1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,812
Tomorrow, I'm going to follow the map!

2
00:00:04,212 --> 00:00:09,141
Don't worry, Grandma. I will be careful.

3
00:00:09,591 --> 00:00:15,664
I'm going to follow the map. I will be careful. Two different ways to talk about the future, in two sentences.

4
00:00:16,264 --> 00:00:20,906
Today you'll learn when to use will, when to use going to, and the mistakes to avoid.

5
00:00:21,856 --> 00:00:23,451
Here's the big picture.

6
00:00:24,051 --> 00:00:28,805
Going to is for plans you made before: I'm going to visit Grandma on Friday.

7
00:00:29,405 --> 00:00:34,212
Will is for decisions you make at the moment of speaking: the phone's ringing. I'll answer it!

8
00:00:34,812 --> 00:00:41,150
Going to is also for predictions with evidence, things you can see coming: look at those clouds. It's going to rain.

9
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:45,925
And will is for opinions about the future: I think you'll love this film.

10
00:00:46,875 --> 00:00:51,161
Going to has three parts: am, is or are, then going to, then the base verb.

11
00:00:51,761 --> 00:00:53,315
I'm going to travel.

12
00:00:53,915 --> 00:00:55,502
She's going to travel.

13
00:00:56,102 --> 00:00:57,657
They're going to travel.

14
00:00:58,257 --> 00:01:02,538
For the negative, add not: she isn't going to travel. I'm not going to travel.

15
00:01:03,638 --> 00:01:07,937
The sun is setting. Mia and Whiskers are going to walk home before it gets dark.

16
00:01:08,887 --> 00:01:13,733
Will is even easier. It's the same for every subject, and it's followed by the base verb.

17
00:01:14,333 --> 00:01:15,349
We'll help you.

18
00:01:15,949 --> 00:01:18,003
It'll be fine. No s, no ing.

19
00:01:18,603 --> 00:01:21,197
The negative is won't: I won't tell anyone.

20
00:01:21,797 --> 00:01:24,437
And for questions, start with will: will you come?

21
00:01:25,387 --> 00:01:27,336
Will has some other jobs, too.

22
00:01:27,936 --> 00:01:30,202
Promises: I will always remember you.

23
00:01:30,802 --> 00:01:33,385
Offers: that bag looks heavy. I'll carry it.

24
00:01:33,985 --> 00:01:36,446
Requests: will you open the window, please?

25
00:01:37,046 --> 00:01:40,753
And quick decisions, like in a restaurant: I'll have the chicken, please.

26
00:01:41,353 --> 00:01:45,392
In everyday speaking, we usually say the short form: I'll, you'll, she'll.

27
00:01:46,292 --> 00:01:51,221
Don't worry, Grandma. I will be careful.

28
00:01:51,671 --> 00:01:54,248
How do native speakers really say these?

29
00:01:54,848 --> 00:01:57,720
Will becomes a short l sound: I'll, you'll, she'll, we'll.

30
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:04,269
Going to often sounds like gonna: I'm gonna, it's gonna, we're gonna. You can say it, but don't write it in exams.

31
00:02:04,869 --> 00:02:10,661
And be careful with won't and want. Won't has an o sound. Want has an a sound. I won't go. I want to go.

32
00:02:11,261 --> 00:02:15,129
Gonna is for speaking only. In writing, always use going to.

33
00:02:16,229 --> 00:02:20,459
Look at the river! The stones are wet. Mia is going to slip! Whiskers, I'll help you!

34
00:02:21,409 --> 00:02:24,842
Questions. With going to, move am, is or are to the front.

35
00:02:25,442 --> 00:02:28,803
Are you going to study tonight? Yes, I am. Or, no, I'm not.

36
00:02:29,403 --> 00:02:31,551
Is it going to rain? Yes, it is.

37
00:02:32,151 --> 00:02:35,949
With will, start with will: will you help me? Yes, I will. Or, no, I won't.

38
00:02:36,549 --> 00:02:39,367
What are you going to do? I'm going to call Grandma.

39
00:02:40,267 --> 00:02:43,542
Will you come with me, Whiskers?

40
00:02:43,992 --> 00:02:46,769
These words tell us we're talking about the future.

41
00:02:47,369 --> 00:02:49,910
Tomorrow. Tonight. Next week. Next year.

42
00:02:50,510 --> 00:02:53,407
Soon. In two days. That means two days from now.

43
00:02:54,007 --> 00:02:58,187
And one day, which means some time in the future: one day, I'll be a pilot.

44
00:02:59,137 --> 00:03:01,018
Let's fix the common mistakes.

45
00:03:01,618 --> 00:03:05,149
I will to go tomorrow. No to after will: I will go tomorrow.

46
00:03:05,749 --> 00:03:08,561
She wills come. Will never takes s: she will come.

47
00:03:09,161 --> 00:03:12,362
I going to study. Don't forget am: I'm going to study.

48
00:03:12,962 --> 00:03:19,128
Tomorrow I go to the doctor. For a plan, say: tomorrow I'm going to the doctor, or I'm going to go to the doctor.

49
00:03:19,728 --> 00:03:24,682
I will call you when I will arrive. After when, use the present: I'll call you when I arrive.

50
00:03:25,632 --> 00:03:28,061
Now you. Listen, then say it out loud.

51
00:03:28,961 --> 00:03:31,004
I'm going to visit my grandma.

52
00:03:34,204 --> 00:03:35,632
It's going to rain.

53
00:03:38,432 --> 00:03:39,485
I'll help you.

54
00:03:42,185 --> 00:03:43,468
I won't forget.

55
00:03:46,168 --> 00:03:47,649
Will you come with me?

56
00:03:50,599 --> 00:03:53,466
One more story. Listen for will, and going to.

57
00:03:54,566 --> 00:04:01,640
Mia shows Grandma the map. Grandma smiles. I think it will be a great adventure, she says. But you're going to need a warm jacket.

58
00:04:02,540 --> 00:04:06,152
Tomorrow, I'm going to follow the map!

59
00:04:06,752 --> 00:04:12,788
The next morning, Mia walks to the hills with a big smile. It's going to be a beautiful day, she thinks. And it will be.

60
00:04:14,602 --> 00:04:17,400
Quiz time. Five questions, five seconds each.

61
00:04:18,350 --> 00:04:21,466
Number 1. Look at those black clouds! It blank rain.

62
00:04:27,266 --> 00:04:30,322
Is going to. We can see the evidence: the clouds.

63
00:04:31,222 --> 00:04:34,172
Number 2. The phone is ringing. I blank answer it!

64
00:04:39,972 --> 00:04:41,892
I'll. A quick decision, now.

65
00:04:42,792 --> 00:04:45,034
Number 3. She will blank us tomorrow.

66
00:04:50,834 --> 00:04:53,034
Visit. After will, the base verb.

67
00:04:53,934 --> 00:04:56,604
Number 4. I blank going to study tonight.

68
00:05:02,404 --> 00:05:04,528
Am. I am going to study tonight.

69
00:05:05,428 --> 00:05:08,120
Number 5. I'll call you when I blank home.

70
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:16,410
Get. After when, use the present simple.

71
00:05:17,310 --> 00:05:24,623
Let's remember. Going to is for plans and for predictions you can see. Will is for quick decisions, promises, offers and opinions.

72
00:05:25,223 --> 00:05:31,749
Going to needs am, is or are. Will is followed by the base verb, with no to and no s. And won't means will not.

73
00:05:32,349 --> 00:05:36,163
Finally, after when, use the present: I'll call you when I arrive.

74
00:05:37,113 --> 00:05:44,543
Your homework: write three plans for next weekend, with going to, and two predictions about your future, with will. Post them in the comments.

75
00:05:45,143 --> 00:05:48,132
Subscribe, and I'll see you in the next lesson. Bye!

